Nectarine: optional discard of colour attachment loads (DXVK 1.10.x / Gcenx DXVK-macOS)

DXVK hardcodes VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_LOAD for every colour attachment, so on a
tile-based GPU every render pass reads back a target it may be about to overwrite.
Gated behind DXVK_X_DISCARD_LOADS=1.

STATUS: verified to work (attachment loads drop to zero, tile traffic halves), but only
measured on a synthetic benchmark, where it gained ~2% because that test is fill-rate
bound. NOT yet validated on a real game -- our from-source DXVK builds run the synthetic
probe but fail to host real games (see README, Known issues). Unsafe as a blanket
setting: passes that blend onto existing contents will start from undefined contents.

--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
@@ resetRenderPassOps
       if (renderTargets.color[i].view != nullptr) {
+        // NECTARINE: skip the attachment load on tile GPUs when enabled.
+        static const int discardLoads = getenv("DXVK_X_DISCARD_LOADS") ? 1 : 0;
         renderPassOps.colorOps[i] = DxvkColorAttachmentOps {
-            VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_LOAD,
+            discardLoads ? VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_DONT_CARE : VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_LOAD,
             renderTargets.color[i].layout,
             renderTargets.color[i].layout };
